# social-gopher Go project

## Package map

- `cmd/social-gopher` — CLI composition root only (flags, wiring, exit codes).
- `internal/catalog` — load/validate/filter `sites.json`.
- `internal/scan` — concurrent probes and existence classifiers.
- `internal/report` — terminal printer and CSV export.
- `internal/transport` — HTTP client, proxy/Tor dial options.
- `internal/torrun` — optional system Tor process lifecycle.
- `data/sites.json` — curated catalog (embedded at build time).

Do not put business logic in `cmd`. Do not introduce new top-level packages without a clear boundary.

## Style and tooling

- Match [`.golangci.yml`](.golangci.yml): 80-column `lll` / `golines`, `gofmt`, `goimports`.
- Prefer table-driven tests. Avoid new dependencies unless clearly justified.
- For idiomatic Go style and SOLID package design, use the existing skills
  `.agents/skills/google-go-style-guide` and `.agents/skills/solid-go-design`
  instead of restating them here.
